{"description":"Expose a versioned, language-agnostic machine protocol (JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio, optional local unix socket) so any consumer can drive steward: initialize (version + capabilities), plan, step/run, resume, cancel, approve, status, shutdown — with idempotency keys and deterministic responses. The protocol is the product boundary; the engine stays in `internal/*`. Loop wiring is owned by sto:steward-run-command; this work item depends on it and does not re-implement the loop — it adapts the same engine over the protocol.","acceptanceCriteria":"Protocol version is negotiated at initialize and evolves additively only. | Methods are deterministic and idempotency keys make retries safe (no duplicate effects). | A consumer can complete a full cycle (initialize -\u003e plan -\u003e run -\u003e status -\u003e shutdown) over stdio. | Golden request/response transcripts are pinned and tested. | The protocol reuses the loop owned by steward-run-command (no duplicated loop wiring)."}